{# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   The timeline itself: the line, and the ordered list of steps along it.

   An <ol> rather than a stack of <div>: a timeline is ordered by definition,
   and the list is what lets a screen reader announce how many steps there are
   and which one is being read.

   The four layouts all include this partial and differ only by `layout`, which
   becomes a BEM modifier. The line, the alternating sides and the horizontal
   scroll are CSS, so a project can restyle or add a layout without touching
   the markup.

   Parameters:
     - layout : alternate | left | right | horizontal
     - steps  : the list of steps
     - plus every parameter `_item.html.twig` reads
   ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── #}

{% set stepList = steps is defined and steps is iterable ? steps : [] %}

{% if stepList|length > 0 %}
    <div class="iw-block-timeline iw-block-timeline--{{ layout|default('alternate') }}">
        {# Decorative: the line is drawn here rather than as a border on the list
           so it can stop at the first and last markers instead of running past
           them. #}
        <div class="iw-block-timeline__line" aria-hidden="true"></div>

        <ol class="iw-timeline">
            {% for step in stepList %}
                {% if step.type|default('step') == 'step' %}
                    {% include '@ItechWorldSuluTailwindTheme/blocks/timeline/_item.html.twig' with {
                        step: step,
                        index: loop.index,
                        dotContent: dotContent|default('icon'),
                        dateMode: dateMode|default('text'),
                        dateFormat: dateFormat|default('month_year'),
                        cardRadius: cardRadius|default(''),
                        imageRadius: imageRadius|default(''),
                        ctaView: stepsView[loop.index0].ctaButtons|default([]),
                        titleAlignment: titleAlignment|default('left')
                    } only %}
                {% endif %}
            {% endfor %}
        </ol>
    </div>
{% endif %}
